e change in goodness of fit (&#x00394;&#x003c7;<sup>2</sup>), and the change in total variance were estimated. MZ and DZ pair correlations are shown for the baseline model including all covariates, and after dropping each.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t4-ehp0115-001224" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Tests of alternative models of sources of variation in erythrocyte lead after adjustment for covariates.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="4" align="center" rowspan="1">Proportions of variance<hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02013;2LL</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">df</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Compared against</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x00394;&#x003c7;<sup>2</sup></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x00394;df</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>p</italic>-Value</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A% (95% CI)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">C% (95% CI)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">D% (95% CI)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">E% (95% CI)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ACE</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02013;2,019.93</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2,828</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">42.5 (23&#x02013;48)</t